<div class="article-body">

<p>I spent $47 on salad greens last month. Then I grew $200 worth of microgreens from a single $13 setup in my kitchen. That's not a typo. One 1020 tray cost me $3.50 in materials and produced enough microgreens to fill 12 clamshell containers. At my local co-op, those sell for $4 each.</p>

<p>Microgreens are the fastest, cheapest way to grow food indoors. No pumps, no electricity (except a cheap LED light), no complicated nutrients. Seeds to harvest in 7 to 14 days. And they're one of the few things you can actually make money on if you grow extra.</p>

<p>This is the guide I wish I had 6 months ago when I killed my first tray by overwatering it. I'll tell you exactly where I screwed up so you don't have to learn the same way.</p>

<h2 id="why">1. Why Microgreens?</h2>

<p>Here's the number that made me switch from growing lettuce to microgreens: a single 1020 tray costs $3.50 in materials and produces $30 to $50 worth of greens. That's a <strong>1,000% ROI in 2 weeks.</strong> Name one other thing you can grow indoors that does that.</p>

<p>Nutritionally, microgreens are a cheat code. A study from the Journal of Agricultural and Food Chemistry found that microgreens contain <strong>4 to 40 times more nutrients</strong> than their mature counterparts. Red cabbage microgreens have 40x more vitamin E and 6x more vitamin C than full grown red cabbage. You eat a handful and you've covered your micronutrients for the day.</p>

<p><strong>The best part?</strong> You don't need a backyard, a green thumb, or expensive gear. I grew my first successful tray on a bookshelf under a $20 LED bulb.</p>

<div class="callout">
  <div class="callout-title">Quick Math. $13 Setup vs Store Prices</div>
  <p>Startup cost: $13 (tray + soil + seeds). First harvest: 7 to 14 days. Value: $30 to $50 per tray. One tray pays for your setup 3x over in the first 2 weeks. Run 4 trays at once and you never buy salad greens again.</p>
</div>

<h2 id="what">2. My Exact $13 Starter Setup</h2>

<p>Here's the exact shopping list. Every item has been tested by me and confirmed by dozens of growers on r/microgreens.</p>

<div class="callout">
  <div class="callout-title">The You Can't Fail Starter Kit. $13 Total</div>
  <p>• <a href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=1020+microgreen+tray+with+dome&tag=tabletopharve-20" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored">1020 microgreen tray with humidity dome</a> ($5.50. Buy the ones with drainage holes)<br>
